  "description": "Splendido, a Belmond hotel, stands above Portofino at Salita Baratta 16, 16034 Portofino, Genoa. The house counts 53 rooms and suites: 48 rooms and suites, five signature suites, and one independent private villa, Villa Beatrice. Belmond operates the hotel. The property telephone is +39 0185 267801. The map on the page places the hotel at 44.305811 north and 9.21148 east.\n\nSignature suites measure 55 to 127 square metres and sleep up to three. Suites measure 60 to 78 square metres and sleep up to three. Junior suites measure 39 to 44 square metres and sleep up to two. Rooms measure 22 to 39 square metres and sleep up to two. The building began as a Benedictine monastery. In the 19th century Baron Baratta bought it and turned it into a summer house. A restoration of three years, by Martin Brudnizki Design Studio, is the most recent work on the hotel, and the Baratta Sedici bar belongs to that work.\n\nLa Terrazza serves Ligurian cooking. Splendido Grill is the second restaurant, and Baratta Sedici is the bar for cocktails. The Dior Spa Splendido sits with Le Jardin des Reves Dior. The hotel has a heated outdoor pool, a tennis court, a gym, a boutique and boat excursions. A complimentary shuttle runs to Splendido Mare in the Piazzetta.\n\nThe hotel gives the drive from Genoa Airport as one hour, and the drive from Santa Margherita-Portofino station as 20 minutes. Event space runs to six venues, with room for up to 60 guests, and four further venues that do not require a buyout of the hotel. The harbour is the view from the hill, and the shuttle is the link down to the square.\n\nThe stay suits Portofino itself: the pool and the spa stay on the hill, and the Piazzetta is a shuttle ride away. Villa Beatrice is the separate house when the booking is for a private villa rather than one of the 53 rooms and suites. A room of 22 to 39 square metres is the smaller key. A signature suite, up to 127 square metres, is the larger one inside the hotel.",
